// The interpreter runs a program's own start and panic fns, as C's main and the runtime
// do (lower.ctx, entry_fns): here a start without std's binary mode, so that on Windows
// "\n" is written as "\r\n", and a panic fn that returns, which traps (132).
// The compiled program's trap is Windows' illegal instruction exception (0xC000001D), or
// SIGILL, which is 132 as a shell reports it; its output is the interpreter's.
//# $ ctxc interp {dir}/hooks.ctx -- a
//# exit: 132
//# [windows] stdout escaped:
//| 2\r
//| main\r
//| index 2 out of bounds for length 219\r
//# [posix] stdout:
//| 2
//| main
//| index 2 out of bounds for length 219
//# $ ctxc run {dir}/hooks.ctx -- a
//# [windows] exit: -1073741795
//# [posix] exit: 132
//# [windows] stdout escaped:
//| 2\r
//| main\r
//| index 2 out of bounds for length 219\r
//# [posix] stdout:
//| 2
//| main
//| index 2 out of bounds for length 219
